    "local_rerun": {
      "status": "answered",
      "answer": "If there is no augmenting path, let S be the vertices reachable from s in the residual graph and T be the rest. No residual edge crosses from S to T, so original edges from S to T are saturated and edges from T to S carry zero flow. Thus the flow\u2019s value equals the capacity of this s\u2013t cut. Since every cut\u2019s capacity is an upper bound on any flow, the flow is maximum.",
